            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of clopidogrel and aspigrel on ectopic cardiac activity in patients with unstable angina pectoris].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The coronary circulation dysfunction in patients with unstable angina pectoris causes development of ventricular and supraventricular cardiac rhythm disorders. Findings from the current study suggest that antianginal therapy of patients with acute coronary syndrome which includes antiaggregant and anticoagulant is effective in the treatment of extrasystolic arrhythmias.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
